ent on to explain that she would use  her power to absorb all living creatures  with her roots  hoping to become the ultimate life form  the planet itself  in the process all humans would be  sucked into her and become one with her  along with the whole planet  now i know that she hasn't officially  been called god level but dragon level  is defined as a threat  endangering multiple cities while a god  level threat is defined as a threat  endangering the survival of all humanity  i think it's clearly being suggested  here that psychos  now has the power to endanger the  survival of humanity considering she  could potentially absorb  everyone and even if you ignore the  definitions the entity who gave her this  immense power must be a threat to all of  humanity  if it can pretty much create multiple  powerful beings like psychos  and that's not even getting into its own  full power  so even if it's not confirmed i think  it's clear that we have encountered what  could be considered a god level threat  already  in this chapter tatsumaki has to deal  with the insanely strong psychos who  starts launching deadly energy beams  everywhere  while trying to protect people and make  sure the beams don't hit the ground  tatsumaki spots king running with the  boy hostage  as usual tatsuwaki hilariously assumes  that king is not fighting the monster  because he's decided that tatsumaki's  powers would be more effective  she has no idea that this whole time  he's been more scared and freaked out  than the boy haas that she's trying to  save  as a tsunami caused by psycho threatens  to destroy a city  tatsumaki comes to the rescue a  beautifully illustrated  high-level psychic battle takes place  and it's cool to see tatsumaki being  pushed hard she's the strongest s-class  hero we've seen  while number one hero blast remains a  mystery so seeing her not just wreck  someone in a second is a pretty big deal  tatsumaki sends large boulders after  large  boulders flying at psychos but they're  easily dealt with tatsumaki is bleeding  at this point covered in dirt  while psychos seems completely fine  herself at this point without so much as  a scratch on her  as observing heroes look on at this  battle they can't help but remark  that it looks like the end of the world  and i really can't wait to see this one  animated  psychos appears to sense tatsumaki's  power which seems to give her x-ray  vision that lets her see through rocks  but this was actually a clever trick by  tatsumaki she focused enough power in  one place so that psychos thought she  was there but actually she snuck into  psychosis body  without her realizing it after calling  her bubble boobs  our tatsumaki uses a giant psychic  tornado to rip her apart from the inside  tatsumaki got through her powerful  barrier by going through the tower  directly below her  she disguised herself as the energy  cycles was absorbing  through her flesh roots and thus entered  her body ready to deal devastating  damage  it's interesting how tatsumaki used  psychos ability to sense energy  against her this long battle finally  looks like it's over and tatsumaki  starts extracting the heroes with all  her effort  rather than by using small amounts of  psychic power undetectable to psychos  she has it all mapped out she'll get  them out including the hilariously naked  puripuri prisoner  and then she'll crush the whole hideout  but then bam tatsumaki's hand gets  stabbed  and we see that whatever psychos has  become  is not done yet tatsumaki gets trapped  and then electrocuted  if she looked beat up before she looks  absolutely fried right now  she's hurt so bad that her psychic power  that was gently carrying people ceases  to work  that means that tatsumaki is seriously  damaged and i couldn't help but laugh  when the stoic  and calm atomic samurai's meditative  stillness was interrupted by the very  naked pudipuri prisoner  falling on his face man it just doesn't  get funnier than that that's the anime  version of bruno landing on eminem's  face  but much funnier psychos calls out  tatsumaki for lowering her guard  she proclaims she'll kill her and her  little sister she's got her trapped by  her punctured hands  and prepares to fire a point-blank  attack things do not  look good but a shot is fired from below  and it deflects psychosis's own shot  to her shock it is our boy demon cyborg  aka  jenos who came to the rescue of  tatsumaki who really did seem close to  her end right there  demon cyborg looks cool af and i love  how his path takes the form of a dragon  he launches another attack but is  overpowered yet another s-class hero  getting bested in a way by this new  psychos tatsumaki being her usual tunde  itself  doesn't thank genos for saving her but  gets mad saying king left psychos to her  however genos won't hear it he says  he'll take care of the beams while  tatsumaki  potentially finishes saving all the  endangered heroes including her sister  even jenos thinks that saitama is their  only hope here  jenos immediately decided to go with his  last resort  and use his full power which will only  last 10 seconds  and he wonders if it'll be enough in the  midst of this intense moment we get  cliffhangered  and jump to others tatsumaki's sister  who can sense the power of psychos is  visibly freaking out  saying there are unimaginable forces up  there now this isn't weird for one punch  man an enemy is hyped up and then  saitama is disappointed by how easily he  finishes them off  despite the hype but still i can't help  but enjoy all this talk about  unmeasurable and unimaginable power  meanwhile we jump to saitama and these  panels are completely juxtaposed to the  epic life and death battle we were just  experiencing saitama complains about  being hungry  as he works towards slowly unbearing  flashy flash who doesn't look so flashy  stuck between rocks  i gotta admit i'm starting to grow fond  of this monster who was originally  trying to kill saitama and flashy flash  the conversations and bonding they're  going through is hilarious the monster  tightens a belt around his stomach  like really tight and says that that  helps to lessen the feeling of hunger  at first saitama just thinks he looks  weirder than ever and says he doesn't  understand monsters but he quickly  changes his mind when his stomach keeps  growling from hunger  he proceeds to tighten his belt and he  admits that maybe  it did help a little while the monster  tells him that he told him so this is  like a mundane silly convo that you'd  have  with your friend but it's happening  between saitama and the monster and that  makes the mundane comedic that's pretty  much what one punch man is about  emphasizing the mundane  in a fantastical superhero world where  you don't expect to find it  saitama proceeds to say that this  monster must have the ultimate  intellect which draws a parallel to  psychos who claim to have the ultimate  intellect  as she was kicking s-class hero butt and  trying to straight-up end humanity for  her it's the biggest deal for saitama  it's anyone who can help him feel a  little bit less hungry  the monster wants to include flashy  flash so that all three of them look  ridiculous with super tight belts but  flashy flash is not amused  and wants no part of it he's a dude who  unlike saitama takes himself way too  seriously and is very concerned with his  hero image which you'll see with many  heroes in this world  while flashy flash thanks god that no  one is around to see him in such an  embarrassing situation  cytomind the monster continue to work  and talk about what saitama is going to  eat later  they appear to settle on curry and so  this chapter that began so action-packed  and intense ends with the slow tedious  work of lifting rocks  and a conversation about curry and  although i want to know what happened  with the fight i welcome such  contrasting moments  it's true that even when we're living  our dreams like saitama is by being a  hero for fun we still spend a lot of our  time  thinking about practical everyday stuff  like what we're gonna eat later  and having to do tedious stuff here and  there the fact that one punch man can  combine the shonen genre we love and  find so entertaining with the less  glamorous realities of everyday life  makes it entertaining relatable bizarre  and absolutely hilarious all at the same  time  can't wait for more humor and more  action on the next one  let me know what you think is gonna  happen next are tatsumaki who appeared  to be in awful shape at some points  and genos gonna be able to pull off the  w without saitama  or is saitama gonna have to show up and  if he does how easy is it gonna be for  him to win  that is the question and give me any  theories you have about this god figure  he's as mysterious as blast at this  point  so many interesting loose ends that i  can't wait to see tied up  if you did enjoy this one punch man  review and want to keep them coming the  best thing you can do is smash that like  button until it is blue if you haven't  be sure to subscribe and this is crucial  hit that notification bell and select  all  or you will miss future one punch man  videos you can check out my existing one  punch man playlist as you wait for the  next review  where you'll find videos about the  s-class heroes a-class heroes  and on all known dragon and god level  threats i'll link that playlist in the  description  feel free to leave suggestions for one  punch man videos you are dying to see  in the comments a very special thank you  goes to our patrons over on patreon who  help make videos like this one possible  first and foremost i want to thank the  patron of legend the one acknowledged by  lord twigo himself  alpha sigma and are the one to your  patrons the ones who stand atop  all clans stephen and grotta alola  nothing the world  steelers acquire respect pate hepa  jonathan king brandon of isles papa  smurf  emp